2026-06-22 15:14:43,997 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-22 15:14:43,997 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: To address the client's requirements, our approach at Faber IA involves designing the AI components of the Atelier platform to prioritize explainability, traceability, and compliance. 

Our AI solution is grounded in a retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) core approach, ensuring that every answer generated is based on passages retrieved from the client's controlled corpus and cites those passages. This grounding principle aligns with the need for answers to be contextualized and grounded in cited sources.

For explainability and traceability, our platform provides features such as source citations, retrieved passages, retrieval traces, and logs of every interaction for posterior audit. These features are built into the workflow, ensuring that professionals can validate and sign off on deliverables, maintaining professional secrecy and reliability of figures.

Compliance with regulatory constraints is ensured through our capability to work with a large volume of regulatory and methodological reference material, including accounting standards, tax doctrine, the commercial code, collective bargaining agreements for payroll, internal procedures, and methodology guides. Our platform can be configured to refrain from producing ungrounded numeric claims and to flag missing sources rather than guess, ensuring reliability and traceability of outputs.

The choice between our sovereign European open-weight model (self-hosted) and top-tier proprietary models (via API) is made per engagement, trading off performance against explainability and sovereignty. This flexibility allows us to meet specific client needs regarding data sovereignty and compliance with GDPR, ensuring that all figures are traceable to a source document and that sensitive data is protected through encryption or pseudonymisation where relevant.

Our iterative methodologies involve corpus curation with the firm's experts, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and an evaluation loop. This approach ensures that our solution integrates well with the client's production tools, such as accounting production software, payroll software, and document management (GED), and supports their professionals in daily activities like retrieval of regulatory and methodological information, drafting professional documents, and handling client files.

By focusing on these aspects, we can provide an AI assistance solution that meets the client's requirements for improving productivity and quality while preserving professional secrecy, avoiding decisional autonomy, and ensuring compliance with regulatory constraints.
